{"canonical_record":{"canonical_payload_sha256":"e220ae1e03964827f460b85550880b29cf57df7299122c8e07753a39ac5940d7","full_review_record_id":"fullrev_9cc51d890072f620471c9efe701712e00f28378515db3ac9ee778c684076e3e2","overall_assessment":"The paper presents a technical contribution to reinforcement learning but fails to meet modern policy and compliance standards for anonymity and broader impact disclosure. The explicit inclusion of author names, affiliations, and emails constitutes a clear violation of double-blind review policies. Additionally, the absence of a dedicated ethics or broader impact section, while not uncommon for 2017 submissions, represents a gap in responsible AI documentation. Data usage is compliant with standard practices for synthetic benchmarks.","paper_id":"B1GOWV5eg","paper_identity_sha256":"ca70bdacc71924d359a776dcb825d70f370617994b47cc2ba4093a7ff4a9d0f9","prompt_identity_sha256":"76add170a709f5577bad74a847300a652b068692741817572e3d78f4df53ab36","raw_response_sha256":"b94770d807129deb72b09d56e5df03eb696abdfd46d2d51cf45177e975f3e7af","request_identity_sha256":"463c40c24f4f1afd8bb36027f7c423cc5c86965c6eb776ab9077c14c2f912618","reviewer_identity_sha256":"6832030d37bc6b05f4de12f913ecdea182594ad5d7ac3dcd33edcb54d7bd3a1a","role":"POL","schema_version":"agentreview-full-review-corpus-v2","structural_context_sha256":"ec8cc86da9d81ce8a38b5be410cca5062f602d489d08646f9fd3ed8657b0909d","subdimension_sections":[{"paper_anchor_ids":[],"review_text":"The paper does not include a dedicated section on ethics, fairness, or potential harms. As a methodological contribution to reinforcement learning, the primary ethical considerations involve the responsible use of computational resources and the potential for dual-use in autonomous control systems. The authors do not discuss these aspects, which is common for technical papers of this era but represents a gap in modern responsible AI compliance. There are no specific claims of bias mitigation or fairness evaluation, which are not directly applicable to the core algorithmic contribution but are increasingly expected in broader impact statements.","subdimension_id":"POL-ETH"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-002","SRC-035"],"review_text":"The experiments utilize standard public benchmarks: Atari 2600, MuJoCo, and TORCS. These environments are widely used in the research community and do not involve personally identifiable information (PII) or sensitive private data. The paper does not explicitly state the licensing terms for the specific software implementations used (e.g., the A3C implementation from GitHub), but the use of open-source code for research purposes is standard practice. No privacy violations or data consent issues are apparent as the data is synthetic game/simulation data.","subdimension_id":"POL-DAT"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-001","SRC-035"],"review_text":"The paper explicitly lists the authors' names (Sahil Sharma, Aravind S. Lakshminarayanan, Balaraman Ravindran) and their affiliation (Indian Institute of Technology, Madras) on the title page. It also provides direct email addresses ({sahil, ravi}@cse.iitm.ac.in, aravindsrinivas@gmail.com). Additionally, the acknowledgments section thanks specific individuals by name (Volodymr Mnih, Aravind Rajeswaran) and mentions specific institutional resources (ILDS at IIT Madras). These details clearly violate double-blind review policies by revealing the identities of the authors and their institutional affiliations.","subdimension_id":"POL-ANO"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-006","SRC-009","SRC-037"],"review_text":"The paper cites relevant prior work, including the authors' own previous work (Lakshminarayanan et al., 2016) and other contemporary research (Mnih et al., 2016a; Durugkar et al., 2016). The content appears to be original, presenting a new framework (FiGAR) that builds upon existing methods. There is no evidence of plagiarism or dual submission within the visible text. The citations are appropriate for the claims made regarding the novelty of the factored policy representation.","subdimension_id":"POL-PLG"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-035"],"review_text":"The paper lacks a formal 'Broader Impact' statement or a checklist for societal considerations, which are now standard requirements for many venues. While the work has potential applications in autonomous systems, the paper does not discuss the broader societal implications, safety concerns, or environmental impact of the computational resources used. The acknowledgments mention the use of open-source implementations and institutional compute resources, but do not provide explicit license compliance details or IRB approvals (though IRB is not typically required for synthetic game data). The absence of a structured impact statement is a weakness in terms of modern compliance standards.","subdimension_id":"POL-IMP"}]},"disposition":"CANONICAL_FULL_REVIEW_COMMITTED","item_commit_sha256":"2c7f0c2bce42a4532975789d5a8972918f631fb3b2021ba05fa7f7cdd4c48af5","paper_id":"B1GOWV5eg","paper_ordinal":6,"raw_attempts":[{"assistant_content_base64":"","assistant_content_sha256":"b94770d807129deb72b09d56e5df03eb696abdfd46d2d51cf45177e975f3e7af","attempt_index":0,"error":"","finish_reason":"stop","paper_id":"B1GOWV5eg","raw_provider_response_base64":"","raw_provider_response_sha256":"a350009a4e7dbe7c020bf3a4d962400d0aa9a3c084d50ed654ec008c7828dd29","request_identity_sha256":"463c40c24f4f1afd8bb36027f7c423cc5c86965c6eb776ab9077c14c2f912618","role":"POL","schema_version":"no-memory-full-review-corpus-build-v2","usage":{"completion_tokens":965,"prompt_tokens":18845,"prompt_tokens_details":null,"total_tokens":19810},"valid":true}],"request_identity_sha256":"463c40c24f4f1afd8bb36027f7c423cc5c86965c6eb776ab9077c14c2f912618","role":"POL","role_ordinal":4,"schema_version":"corpus-build-bootstrap-checkpoint-v1"}